Inkling 2 Mini on vLLM for Ampere GPUs
Copyright 2026 peaster

This repository contains no vLLM, Triton or model binaries. The Dockerfile
downloads the official vllm/vllm-openai image and one official vLLM wheel at
build time.

Portions derived from other projects:

- apply_sm86_patch.py and tools/widen_test_gates.py quote short passages of
  vLLM (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm) and Triton (MIT,
  https://github.com/triton-lang/triton) as patch anchors and as the text
  that replaces them.
- patches/sm86-tune.diff modifies files of vLLM (Apache-2.0, copyright the
  vLLM contributors). Part of it is adapted from
  snailbrainx/inkling-2-mini-sm80 (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 snailbrainx,
  https://github.com/snailbrainx/inkling-2-mini-sm80): the Ampere tiles of
  the low-row GEMV kernel, the one-launch q/k/v projection, the loop
  controller kernels, the drafter's Markov fold on the GEMV, the draft
  length range, the far-block loop of the attention kernel and the
  one-kernel moe_align_block_size. Changed here: a shared-memory fit so
  the tiles run on sm_86, switches for each tuning, and the expert-GEMM
  alignment limited to the batch sizes where its output is identical to
  the compiled op's. Added here: expert-GEMM kernel configs, router
  and attention tiles measured on sm_86, the draft length chosen per step
  from recent acceptance, and the reduced draft vocabulary.
  Another part is adapted from Pento95/HyperInkling (Apache-2.0,
  https://github.com/Pento95/HyperInkling): the conv-state cache manager
  that backs only each step's tail (SconvStateManager) and the conv
  kernel's skipped stores into the null block. Added to it here: conv-state
  checkpoints at the prefix-cache retention interval, and the switch.
- tools/tests/conftest.py reproduces three fixtures from vLLM's
  tests/conftest.py.
- tools/gsm8k_eval.py follows the chat protocol of vLLM's
  tests/evals/gsm8k/gsm8k_eval.py.
- tools/tune/published_protocols.py re-implements the benchmark protocols
  of agent2x0r/inkling2-sm86-kernels (MIT) and Pento95/HyperInkling and
  sends their prompts; no code from either is included.
- patches/draft_vocab_rank.json is a list of token ids in rank order and
  contains no text. The counts behind it came from this model's own output
  and from wikitext-2 (CC BY-SA 3.0), HellaSwag (MIT), War and Peace (public
  domain, Project Gutenberg), vLLM's Python source (Apache-2.0), ggml's C
  source (MIT) and a private tree of configs and docs.
- tools/tune/more_protocols.py re-implements the benchmark protocols of
  lulakien/inkling2-mini-3090-recipe and skyne98/inkling-ingine-3090 from
  the prompts and parameters they publish; it contains none of their code.
